# ADR-0031 — paths excluded from the substantive-diff
# count enforced by tools/ci/check-pr-size.sh. One pathspec per
# line; `#` comments and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Rationale: lockfile updates, generated code, vendored fixtures,
# and pure rename diffs do not represent reviewer-load. They
# legitimately produce large diffs that should not push a PR
# over the 1500-line cap.

# Lock files (regenerated, not authored). Both forms are needed: a leading
# `**/` matches nested paths only, so it never covers the root file, and a
# bare name never covers a nested one. Verified against this diff, where
# `**/composer.lock` alone still left the root lockfile counted.
composer.lock
**/composer.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
**/pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
**/package-lock.json
yarn.lock
**/yarn.lock

# Generated API snapshot (regenerated by composer api:snapshot)
tools/api/public-api.snapshot.json

# Tool baselines. Every one is written by the tool that reads it — phpstan,
# deptrac, the substitutability and wiring assertions, the benchmark floor —
# so a diff here is machine output, not something to read line by line. The
# debt they record is guarded by the ratchet tests, not by this cap.
tools/php/*-baseline.json
tools/php/*-baseline.neon
tests/Unit/Integrity/*-baseline.json

